.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt BUS_MATCH_DEVICE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm bus_match_device
.Nd find the best matched driver for a device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/kern/bus.h
.Ft struct driver *
.Fn bus_match_device "struct bus_type *bus" "struct device *dev"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn bus_match_device
function iterates over all drivers registered on the specified
.Fa bus
to find a driver that supports the device
.Fa dev .
.Pp
For each driver, the function determines a match using the following precedence:
.Bl -enum
.It
If the driver provides a
.Va match_func
callback, it is invoked.
.It
Otherwise, the bus's
.Va match
callback is invoked.
.El
.Pp
If multiple drivers match the device, the one with the highest
.Va priority
is returned. Ties are broken by selecting the first driver encountered (registration order).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn bus_match_device
function returns a pointer to the best matching
.Ft struct driver
if one is found, or
.Dv NULL
if no driver matches.
.Sh LOCKING
The function acquires and releases the bus's spinlock to safely traverse the driver list.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bus 9 ,
.Xr driver 9 ,
.Xr device 9
